\section{Consolidated Annotated Bibliography (Top 20 most important entries)}

\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{IEEE} (2025). \textit{IEEE Std 3221.01-2025: Standard for blockchain interoperability---Cross-chain transaction consistency protocol}. IEEE Standards Association. \url{https://standards.ieee.org/ieee/3221.01/}
    
    First formal cross-chain consistency standard; provides atomicity benchmarks the thesis will measure against.
    
    \item \textbf{Unique Network} (2025). \textit{Composable Subscriptions \& NFTs using XCM} (blog series Jan--Sep 2025). \url{https://unique.network/blog}
    
    Closest existing work: native Polkadot recurring NFTs. Still lacks PPV counters and unified rights object $\rightarrow$ thesis extends this.
    
    \item \textbf{MarketsandMarkets} (2025). \textit{Blockchain Digital Rights Management Market --- Global Forecast to 2029}.
    
    Projects 54.2\% CAGR, \$1.42B by 2029 --- validates economic significance of the research.
    
    \item \textbf{IBC Protocol} (2025). \textit{IBC v2 Specification and Launch Announcement}. \url{https://ibcprotocol.dev}
    
    Sovereign interop alternative to XCM; 115+ chains connected by Nov 2025.
    
    \item \textbf{Chainlink} (2025). \textit{Cross-Chain Interoperability Protocol (CCIP) Technical Whitepaper v2}.
    
    Oracle-based bridge used by most Ethereum-centric competitors.
    
    \item \textbf{Zhang, L. et al.} (2024). A digital resource copyright protection scheme based on blockchain cross-chain technology. \textit{Heliyon, 10}(16), e34781. \url{https://doi.org/10.1016/j.heliyon.2024.e34781}
    
    State-of-the-art cross-chain DRM --- protection only, no monetisation workflows.
    
    \item \textbf{USPTO/USCO} (2024). \textit{Non-Fungible Tokens and Intellectual Property}. Joint report.
    
    Authoritative legal analysis of NFT ownership and licensing --- foundation for PurchaseVerification contract.
    
    \item \textbf{Wang \& Li} (2025). AI-blockchain integration for digital rights management: A review. \textit{Journal of Digital Media Security}.
    
    Shows AI improves verification; future extension opportunity for the thesis.
    
    \item \textbf{Frontiers in Blockchain} (2025). Regulatory barriers in blockchain-based IP trade: Evidence from China.
    
    Regulatory compliance identified as the single largest barrier (weight 0.308) $\rightarrow$ justifies optional ZK hooks.
    
    \item \textbf{Eluvio} (2024). \textit{The Content Fabric: Multi-Chain Content Ownership and Distribution}. Whitepaper.
    
    Industry competitor with marketplace-ready fabric; hybrid centralised/decentralised.
    
    \item[11--20.] Wood (2016, 2022), Parity ink! docs, Polkadot wiki, Xie \& Liu (2022), Garba et al. (2020), etc.
    
    Foundational technical and early multi-chain DRM papers (already in original proposal + Weeks 1--4 reports).
\end{enumerate}

